{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.BraidingEigenvalueExtraction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.BraidingEigenvalueExtraction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Braided.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Rigid.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic"],"declarations":21,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.braiding_eigenvalue_extraction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.braiding_eigenvalue_extraction","kind":"theorem","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L218-L235","doc":"The full extraction: from eigenvalues + det constraint, derive\nq, the forced antisymmetric eigenvalue, and the Hecke relation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:braiding-eigenvalue-extraction","label":"prop:braiding-eigenvalue-extraction","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.quantum_regime","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.quantum_regime","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L213-L216","doc":"Quantum regime: non-symmetric braiding forces q ≠ 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.classical_limit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.classical_limit","kind":"theorem","line":206,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L206-L211","doc":"Classical limit: symmetric braiding (c² = id) forces q = 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.hecke_polynomial_roots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.hecke_polynomial_roots","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L184-L204","doc":"**Both eigenvalues of `c_{V,V}` are roots of the Hecke polynomial**, in\nits `q`-cleared form.\n\nThe narrative polynomial is `(X - q)(X + q⁻¹)`. Multiplying the second\nfactor by the unit `q` clears the inverse without changing the root set,\ngiving `(X - q)(qX + 1)` — well-typed over `R_q`, where `⁻¹` is not\navailable (see `symm_mul_neg_anti`).\n\nRoot set is unchanged because `q` is a unit (`isUnit_lamSym`): `qX + 1`\nand `X + q⁻¹` differ by that unit factor, so they vanish together. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.isUnit_lamSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.isUnit_lamSym","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L175-L182","doc":"Consequently `λ₊` is a **unit** of `R_q`, witnessed by `-λ₋`.\n\nOver a field this would be the content of `lamSym ≠ 0`; over a ring\n\"invertible\" is strictly stronger than \"nonzero\", and it is the stronger\nstatement that the braiding actually supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.symm_mul_neg_anti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.symm_mul_neg_anti","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L154-L173","doc":"**The antisymmetric eigenvalue is the negated inverse of the symmetric\none**, stated multiplicatively.\n\nThe narrative form is `λ₋ = -q⁻¹`. That form is **not well-typed here**:\nthe ground ring is `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`, which has no `Inv` instance — the\n*indeterminate* `q` is invertible in `R_q`, but a general element is not,\nso there is no `⁻¹` operation to apply to `lamSym`. The equivalent\nproduct identity carries the same content and survives the ring:\n`-λ₋` is a two-sided inverse of `λ₊`.\n\nThis is exactly `det_constraint` rearranged; the `⁻¹` spelling added no\ninformation over a field either. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.q","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L149-L152","doc":"The deformation parameter q extracted from braiding eigenvalues.\nBy convention, q := lamSym (the symmetric eigenvalue). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.det_constraint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.det_constraint","kind":"theorem","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L147-L147","doc":"Hecke product condition: lamSym · lamAnti = -1.\nThis is the product of roots of the Hecke polynomial\n(T - q)(T + q⁻¹) = T² - (q - q⁻¹)T - 1, whose constant\nterm is -1.  Note: this is *not* the 4D determinant of\nc_{V,V} on V ⊗ V (which would be q³·(-q⁻¹) = -q²), but\nrather the product of the two *distinct* eigenvalues. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.lamAnti_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.lamAnti_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L140-L140","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.lamSym_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.lamSym_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L139-L139","doc":"The braiding is non-degenerate: both eigenvalues are nonzero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.lamAnti","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.lamAnti","kind":"def","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L137-L137","doc":"Eigenvalue on the antisymmetric summand Λ²V ≅ 𝟙. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.lamSym","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.lamSym","kind":"def","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L135-L135","doc":"Eigenvalue on the symmetric summand S²V. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidingEigenvalueData","kind":"structure","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L122-L147","doc":"The braiding eigenvalue data for a rank-2 fundamental object V.\nThe braiding c_{V,V} : V ⊗ V → V ⊗ V has two eigenvalues:\nλ₊ = q on the symmetric summand S²V (dim 3),\nλ₋ = -q⁻¹ on the antisymmetric summand Λ²V ≅ 𝟙 (dim 1).\n\nThis structure encodes the spectral data of the braiding as\ncategorical invariants.  The fields are the *output* of the\nspectral decomposition axiom above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.spectral_decomposition_of_braiding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.spectral_decomposition_of_braiding","kind":"axiom","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L104-L115","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.is_symmetric_braiding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.is_symmetric_braiding","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L82-L86","doc":"The braiding is symmetric iff c² = id. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.braiding_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.braiding_squared","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L74-L80","doc":"The braiding squared: (β_ V V).hom ≫ (β_ V V).hom.\nWhen this equals 𝟙, the braiding is symmetric (classical case).\nWhen it doesn't, we're in the quantum regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.braiding_is_automorphism","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.braiding_is_automorphism","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L66-L72","doc":"In a braided monoidal category, the braiding on V ⊗ V is an\nautomorphism (isomorphism from V ⊗ V to itself). This is\nimmediate from `BraidedCategory`: `β_ V V` is an `Iso`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L58-L58","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/braiding-eigenvalue-extraction.lean#L55-L57","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}